From 27699e25b887dd7e7fbc2c53c990a8b4e4e71086 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:40:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Runner: seats drive Sonic Riders' 8 racers (phase 2
 prototype)

With SRNP_RACERS=1, seat k of the relay drives racer k of Sonic Riders
(GXEE8P). Each racer's control byte (+0xBC: 0 human, 1 CPU) picks the
function that writes its controls; the human one reads the controller
structure the racer points to. The runner fills one structure per seat
the way the game fills its own (main.dol 0x80006778, rumble left out;
SRNP_PADCHECK=1 compares both, 0 differences over 1200 frames), in low
memory the game leaves at zero, points the racer to it and makes it
human. A seat can give its racer back to the AI for the rest of the race
(the game's CPUs only: the AI of a racer that was human when the race
was set up crashes the game). When the game makes a racer CPU itself
(finish line), the runner leaves it. Viewport 0's camera follows the
local seat's racer.

The relay client takes several local seats (SRNP_SEAT=3,4), racing test
inputs (SRNP_INPUT=course:<seed>), a checksum of the 8 racers without the
fields that follow the camera, and SRNP_CKDUMP to dump the racers at
each checksum.

